-- lib/compile/runs.cub — runs of a step function as a relation, and the meaning of bytes
-- (lib/compile/meaning.cub) reduced to one run.
--
-- Runs stp stop k s s2: k steps of stp lead from s to s2, each outcome a value, and none of the k
-- steps is taken from a state whose rip is stop. Runs compose (runs-cat). run-to (meaning.cub)
-- from s, whatever its fuel, either runs out or stops at s2 when a run reaches s2 at stop
-- (run-to-runs). So bytes are correct for f at an argument as soon as one run from the call's
-- state reaches the return with f's value (correct-at): every other fuel gives f's value too.
-- Everything here is of a step function that is a variable; the model is not unfolded.
